LÖVE @VERSION@ for AROS
====================

LÖVE is a framework for making 2D games in Lua: https://love2d.org
This is a build of LÖVE @VERSION@ (upstream development branch, commit
@COMMIT@) for @SYSTEM@.

Needs
-----

  - @SYSTEM@, nightly build of 2026-11-15 or later
  - OpenGL (Mesa, part of the system)
  - AHI for sound, a TCP/IP stack for network games

Starting a game
---------------

From Workbench:

  - Double-click the love icon and choose the game in the file requester:
    a .love file, or the drawer that holds main.lua (go into the drawer and
    leave the file name empty). A game for Windows that is a single .exe
    made with LÖVE can be chosen as well.
  - Or drop the game's icon on LÖVE's window while it shows no game.
  - To give a game its own icon, type in a Shell:

        love --icon <game.love or drawer with main.lua>

    A double click on the new icon starts the game. For a .love file the
    icon is the file's own; for a game in a drawer it is the icon of
    main.lua inside that drawer. The icon keeps the place of this drawer;
    delete it and make it again after moving this drawer.

From a Shell, with the path of this drawer in front of love:

    Run love <drawer with main.lua>
    Run love <game.love>

Start it with Run: a program that uses OpenGL directly from a Shell disturbs
the commands typed into that Shell afterwards.

Saved games and settings of a game are kept in the Saves drawer beside the
program, one drawer per game. Saves that an earlier revision left in
ENVARC:LOVE/<game> stay there and stay in use; to move them, copy that
drawer into Saves and delete it from ENVARC:LOVE.

What works
----------

Window and fullscreen, drawing (images, shapes, text, canvases, shaders),
keyboard and mouse, sound (WAV, Ogg Vorbis, MP3, FLAC, tracker modules),
game files and .love archives, threads, physics. Games run on LuaJIT.

Network: LuaSocket, ENet and HTTPS requests (require "https"). HTTPS checks
the server's certificate against the system's certificate bundle.

A game that asks for a window larger than the screen gets one that fits.

Known issues
------------

  - Joysticks and video playback are not tested.
  - Without hardware OpenGL the system draws in software and games are slow.
  - ffi.load and ffi.C cannot find functions (AROS has no dlopen).

Please report problems: @REPOSITORY@/issues

